## Context

Section §3 of `slides/manuscript/main.md` describes the capability ladder as a
partial order (DAG), not a total sequence. Stages 3 and 4 are parallel; stage 5
follows both. This claim currently rests on prose and the timeline figure (Fig 4).

A companion figure would make the DAG structure directly visible from the data.

## Proposed figure: two panels

### Panel A — Transition-order matrix (8×8 heatmap)

For each ordered pair (i, j) of capability stages:
- Cell value = fraction of labs where stage i was acquired before stage j
  (conditional on both being acquired)
- Cells near 1.0 → strong empirical ordering
- Cells near 0.5 → parallel / interchangeable
- Cells near 0.0 → reverse ordering observed
- Label N per cell (some transitions have fewer than 5 labs)

### Panel B — Time-gap dot-range plot

For transitions with N ≥ 4:
- Show raw dots (one per lab) + range bar
- X-axis: gap in months between stage i and stage j
- Only high-confidence transitions (N ≥ 4) to avoid false precision
- Caption must label N per transition explicitly

## Data source

`data/capability_timeline.csv` — per-lab, per-stage launch dates for 5 labs
(Anthropic, OpenAI, Mistral, Qwen, DeepSeek).

## Implementation

- New script: `src/aedist/plot_capability_dag.py`
- Output: `inputs/generated/fig_capability_dag.pdf`
- Makefile target wired from `data/capability_timeline.csv`
- Include in §3 as companion to Fig 4

## Honest design constraints

- N=5 labs total; some cells drop to N=2–3
- Panel B only shows cells with N ≥ 4
- "Descriptive historical record, N=5 labs" in caption — no statistical inference
- Raw scatter preferred over means for Panel B

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `plot_capability_dag.py` reads `data/capability_timeline.csv`
- [ ] Panel A: 8×8 heatmap with N labelled per cell
- [ ] Panel B: dot-range for N≥4 transitions only, N labelled
- [ ] Output wired as `inputs/generated/fig_capability_dag.pdf`
- [ ] Makefile target in place
- [ ] Figure included in §3 with caption
- [ ] §3 prose updated to reflect the empirical DAG structure found (notation and parallel/sequential claims follow the data)
- [ ] `make check` passes
